    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0534" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1747</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Guaranty Trust Company of New
                            York to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 16.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">513–27</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Foreign Department</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We have the pleasure to acknowledge receipt
                    of your communication of the 12th instant, and in view of the contents thereof
                    we have advised the President of Nicaragua, through the Manager of the National
                    Bank of Nicaragua, Inc., that we, in conjunction with Messrs. J. &amp; W.
                    Seligman &amp; Co., are prepared to make a loan of $1,000,000.—to the Republic
                    of Nicaragua for the purposes, and under <pb facs="0535" n="433" xml:id="pg433"
                    /> the terms and conditions indicated in the memorandum of the 11th of March,
                    1927, which was sent to you with our letter of the same date.</p>
                <p>We are [etc.]</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guaranty Trust Company of New
                            York</hi>,<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. F.
                        Loree</hi></signed>, <hi rendition="#italic">Vice President</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
